rndis_host/usbnet: RX batching with a deep queue (default 8x / 8x)

Lets the FM350-GL pack several frames per USB transfer (8x RX URB = ~16 KB, ~10
frames) while keeping the usbnet RX ring deep; cuts xHCI interrupts ~8x and
frees CPU0, which was the ~330 Mbps forwarding wall. Needs 901 (copy split),
else the clones of the shared URB buffer cost more than batching saves.
  rndis_host.rndis_rx_urb_mult  - multiply RX URB / advertised max_transfer_size
                                  (lets the modem batch frames per USB transfer)
  usbnet.rx_qlen_mult           - multiply the SuperSpeed RX queue depth so a
                                  larger buffer still keeps many URBs in flight
                                  (usbnet caps total ring bytes, capped here 2MB)
Defaults 8 and 8 (1 = stock). Built-in drivers: params at
/sys/module/{rndis_host,usbnet}/parameters/, applied when the interface binds.
--- a/drivers/net/usb/rndis_host.c	2026-09-02 23:20:25.401324000 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/rndis_host.c	2026-09-02 23:20:25.412675750 +0000
@@ -284,6 +284,14 @@
 	.ndo_validate_addr	= eth_validate_addr,
 };
 
+/* RX batching: enlarge the RNDIS RX URB (and the advertised
+ * max_transfer_size) so the modem may pack several frames per USB transfer.
+ * Pair with usbnet rx_qlen_mult to keep enough URBs in flight (bigger buffers
+ * otherwise shrink the fixed-memory usbnet RX ring). 1 = stock. */
+static unsigned int rndis_rx_urb_mult = 8;
+module_param(rndis_rx_urb_mult, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rndis_rx_urb_mult, "Multiply RNDIS RX URB size (default 8, 1=stock)");
+
 int
